asr-002909
02:51:58.780 --> 02:52:01.280
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: shall be considered equivalent to

asr-002910
02:52:01.280 --> 02:52:09.240
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: marital relationship. My question is, what is the specific statutory basis for the CSC

asr-002911
02:52:09.240 --> 02:52:16.440
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: to make this additional classification? More importantly, Madam Chair, does this not raise

asr-002912
02:52:16.440 --> 02:52:22.480
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: a concern under the fundamental principle that an administrative agency cannot rise

asr-002913
02:52:22.480 --> 02:52:29.620
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: above its enabling law, that the spring cannot rise above its source? If Congress has itself

asr-002914
02:52:29.620 --> 02:52:35.420
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: specifically defined the relationships and degrees covered by the statutory prohibition,

asr-002915
02:52:36.160 --> 02:52:42.280
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: would the CSC's inclusion of common law relationships effectively expand, modify,

asr-002916
02:52:42.280 --> 02:52:49.860
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: or add to a substantive prohibition that Congress itself has prescribed? I fully recognize the

asr-002917
02:52:49.860 --> 02:52:57.120
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: authority of the CSC to promulgate rules and necessary to implement civil service laws.

asr-002918
02:52:57.660 --> 02:52:59.600
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: But where the implementing rule

asr-002919
02:52:59.600 --> 02:53:06.920
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: creates an additional category of persons subject to a legal prohibition, where do we draw the line

asr-002920
02:53:06.920 --> 02:53:14.020
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: between implementation and legislation? Would the Commission agree that while an administrative

asr-002921
02:53:14.020 --> 02:53:21.220
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: agency may fill in the details necessary to carry out a law, it cannot enlarge the scope

asr-002922
02:53:21.220 --> 02:53:28.620
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: of a statutory prohibition or create a new substantive restriction absent clear authority

asr-002923
02:53:28.620 --> 02:53:29.440
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: from Congress?

asr-002924
02:53:29.600 --> 02:53:37.320
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: And finally, if the CSC believes that common law relationship should be covered by the prohibition

asr-002925
02:53:37.320 --> 02:53:44.300
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: on nepotism, should that policy not properly be addressed through legislation rather than

asr-002926
02:53:44.300 --> 02:53:53.460
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: through an administrative rule? I raise this question not to question the objective of

asr-002927
02:53:53.460 --> 02:53:59.580
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: preventing nepotism, but to clarify the limits of administrative rulemaking and to

asr-002928
02:53:59.600 --> 02:54:05.840
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: ensure that the Commission's regulations remain firmly anchored on the law and acted by Congress.

asr-002929
02:54:06.280 --> 02:54:07.060
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Thank you, Madam Chair.

asr-002930
02:54:08.560 --> 02:54:12.160
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: As Comrade Romeo will answer the question, please.

asr-002931
02:54:12.940 --> 02:54:20.900
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: Thank you, Madam Chair. First, we want to recognize the valid position of the Honorable

asr-002932
02:54:20.900 --> 02:54:27.660
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: Congresswoman, and we agree that, of course, if there is no legal basis, we cannot,

asr-002933
02:54:27.660 --> 02:54:29.460
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: by administrative,

asr-002934
02:54:29.600 --> 02:54:38.760
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: fiat, come up with something that will be later found to be prejudicial to persons involved.

asr-002935
02:54:38.760 --> 02:54:45.280
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: But I will beg the indulgence of the honourable members of the committee to also understand

asr-002936
02:54:45.280 --> 02:54:46.920
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: where the commission is coming from.

asr-002937
02:54:47.520 --> 02:54:58.480
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: Nepotism is an offence defined under our laws and the purpose of prohibiting nepotism is

asr-002938
02:54:58.480 --> 02:55:03.400
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: to ensure that appointments in the civil service should only be made according to merit and

asr-002939
02:55:03.400 --> 02:55:12.540
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: fitness and that any form of favoritism is not used as basis for the issuance of an appointment

asr-002940
02:55:12.540 --> 02:55:14.480
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: to any position in government.

asr-002941
02:55:15.800 --> 02:55:19.000
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: Nepotism is a prohibition against appointing relatives.

asr-002942
02:55:20.000 --> 02:55:20.220
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: That is correct.

asr-002943
02:55:20.880 --> 02:55:27.100
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: But the underlying consideration is that if a relative is appointed to a position that

asr-002944
02:55:27.100 --> 02:55:28.460
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: requires merit and fitness,

asr-002945
02:55:28.480 --> 02:55:33.860
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: the consideration is not actually merit and fitness but the relationship itself.

asr-002946
02:55:34.840 --> 02:55:42.740
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: And according to a number of jurisprudence, what cannot be done directly cannot be done indirectly.

asr-002947
02:55:43.260 --> 02:55:52.780
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: If you cannot extend that favoritism to your relative, neither can you extend the same favoritism

asr-002948
02:55:52.780 --> 02:55:58.460
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: to a person who stands in the same place as your relative.

asr-002949
02:55:58.480 --> 02:56:03.200
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: Now, the Civil Service Commission does not come from nothing.

asr-002950
02:56:03.200 --> 02:56:10.400
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: In the previous years, the Supreme Court has also declared as violative of the rule against

asr-002951
02:56:10.400 --> 02:56:13.340
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: nepotism the designation of a relative.

asr-002952
02:56:13.560 --> 02:56:15.100
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: Designation is not an appointment.

asr-002953
02:56:15.720 --> 02:56:20.300
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: And designation is not also covered by the definition of the law on nepotism.

asr-002954
02:56:20.620 --> 02:56:25.500
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: But the Supreme Court, using the same principle that what you cannot do directly, you cannot

asr-002955
02:56:25.500 --> 02:56:27.620
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: do indirectly, also declared.

asr-002956
02:56:28.480 --> 02:56:33.280
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: In the case of Laurel v. CSE, that if you cannot do that by way of appointment, you

asr-002957
02:56:33.280 --> 02:56:37.440
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: cannot also do that by way of designation because the same evil exists.

asr-002958
02:56:37.440 --> 02:56:41.160
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: Madam Chair, that's where the commission is coming from.

asr-002959
02:56:41.160 --> 02:56:45.300
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: We do not want the same evil to exist.

asr-002960
02:56:45.300 --> 02:56:51.760
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: We just use as our basis those previous pronouncements made by the Supreme Court.

asr-002961
02:56:51.760 --> 02:56:54.000
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: What you cannot do directly, you cannot do indirectly.

asr-002962
02:56:54.000 --> 02:56:54.840
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: Madam Chair.

asr-002963
02:56:57.150 --> 02:57:02.230
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Madam Chair, because we're referring this to the common-law partners.

asr-002969
02:57:03.790 --> 02:57:12.290
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: Opo, kasi po yung common-law partners is in the same place as a married couple.

asr-002977
02:57:14.590 --> 02:57:18.970
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: Um, so ang kulang lang po doon kasi ay marriage [unclear].

asr-002983
02:57:18.970 --> 02:57:27.970
CSC Assistant Commissioner Ariel Ronquillo: Pero I think the same relationship exists between and among the parties involved.

